    {
      "key": "d12d5616-1fc9-4fca-a3fa-d5a6bb900ea5",
      "position": 3,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** Click through the animated slide to display the prompts.\n- *Think about an app you use every day. Who do you think made the decisions about how it looks and works?*\n- *What would you want to know about how that happened?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** This is a baseline prompt, not a comprehension check. Students don't need to get the \"right\" answer. Listen for what they already believe: some may say developers, some may say the company, some may say AI. Surface those ideas without correcting them. The goal is to capture where students are starting from — especially any assumptions that AI makes these decisions on its own — so those ideas can be revisited at the end of the unit.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the Key Vocabulary."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "d12d5616-1fc9-4fca-a3fa-d5a6bb900ea5",
        "lesson_activity.key": "030e4cd6-6b8a-4dad-bc3d-cf8798368385"
      }
    },
